          heading: "Worked example: the pre-ship run",
          kind: "example",
          body:
            "A realistic final pass on a dashboard build, in order, with the actual instruments:\n\n```\nBASELINE (Day 1, 45 min)\n  Lighthouse (throttled, 4× runs, take the median)\n    Perf 62 · A11y 88 · SEO 91 · Best practices 87\n  Network, cache disabled:\n    74 requests · 3.9 MB · hero JPEG 2.4 MB · 6 sequential API calls\n  Profiler, record \"switch range 7d → 30d\":\n    StatGrid re-renders 12 components per click; Chart re-renders 9× …\n\nFIX 1 — the image (biggest number first)\n  hero.jpg → hero.avif (2.4 MB → 148 KB) + <picture> with width/height,\n  fetchpriority=\"high\" on the LCP image, lazy on the 8 below-fold cards.\n  Lighthouse Perf: 62 → 84.\n\nFIX 2 — the waterfall\n  const [profile, plan, usage] = await Promise.all([...])   // staircase → one row\n  lift shared course data to the layout instead of refetching per card.\n  Requests: 74 → 41.\n\nFIX 3 — the render loop the log found\n  useEffect(() => setRows(sorted), [rows, sort]) — effect set its own dep.\n  Derived with useMemo instead. Profiler: 9 renders per click → 1.\n\nFIX 4 — measured memoisation only\n  Profiler still showed CourseRow × 100 on every keystroke in the filter.\n  Stabilised props (id primitives, useCallback on onSelect), then memo(CourseRow).\n  Keystroke render: 102 components → 3.\n\nACCESSIBILITY PASS (instruments, not intentions)\n  Keyboard only: full workflow — found focus lost after modal close → fixed with\n    focus return; found the chart's toggle unreachable → it was a div, now a button.\n  axe DevTools: 1 critical (label missing), 4 serious (contrast 2.4:1 on muted text,\n    3 greys lightened to ≥4.5:1; aria-expanded not updated on the disclosure).\n  200% zoom + 320 px: two horizontal scrollbars → minmax(0,1fr) and an image\n    without max-width:100%.\n  prefers-reduced-motion: two transitions disabled.\n\nEDGE-CASE WALK (the written list, with a pen)\n  [] → empty ✓ · [one] → \"1 course\" ✓ · 300-char title → truncates ✓\n  null avatar → initials fallback ✓ · NaN revenue → \"—\" + log ✓\n  offline → error + retry, sidebar still navigable ✓\n  double-click Add → second click ignored while pending ✓\n  expired session mid-save → preserves values, returns after sign-in ✓\n\nSHIP\n  build: 312 KB first-load JS (route-split the chart: 84 KB lazy)\n  git tag v1.0.0 · deploy · test the live URL on a phone on mobile data\n  Lighthouse on the real deployment (not localhost): Perf 94 · A11y 100 · SEO 100\n  README + rollback note (previous tag, how to redeploy)\n```\n\nRead it again as a *method*: baseline with numbers, biggest number first, measure after every fix, accessibility with tools that fail loudly, a written edge-case list rather than memory, and the final verification on the actual deployment — on a phone, on real network — because localhost lies about all three.",
